    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0130" n="116" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg116"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Conference (W and PW)/1–2445</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Report by Mr. Dudley B. Bonsal, of the Office of the
                        Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>),
                        <hi rendition="#italic">on Preparations for the Inter-American Conference on
                        Problems of War and Peace</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-15">February 15,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Attached is memorandum<anchor n="75" xml:id="d76-f1"/> prepared by Larry Duggan
                    and myself listing the questions which were propounded to the Ambassadors
                    regarding the responsibilities and relationships of the Inter-American System
                    and our proposed answers as to the U.S. position to be taken at the Mexico City
                    Conference.</p>


                <xi:include href="d76-a1.xml" xpointer="d76-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
